    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.sessions, mini.extra\n\n### Description\n\nNew picker:\r\n\r\n- `MiniExtra.pickers.sessions`\r\n\r\nI'm aware a `vim.ui.select` implementation exists in `mini.sessions` which `mini.pick` can override with its builtin implementation, but it would be nice to get a better looking one with icons, etc which would also available for those who do not have `mini.sessions` installed.\r\n\r\nSpecifically, for my intended use case, I wanted to use custom mappings for `mini.sessions` to invoke `MiniSessions.delete` from the picker itself.",
